  "selection": {
    "length": 489,
    "text": "Mr Adeyemi —\n\nThere is a key taped above this line. It opens nothing.\n\nI had it cut to a blank that matches no lock anywhere, which cost about a pound and took a morning. I did that because a letter from a stranger has roughly four seconds to survive the walk from your post room to your bin, and an envelope with a key in it does not feel like paper. It feels like an object, and objects get opened.\n\nThat is the whole trick. I would rather tell you than have you work it out on your own.",
    "findResult": true
